“A human will review it” is a useful principle, but it is not a workflow design.
When a small business adds AI to a sales, document, or customer-service process, the risky part is usually not the model call. It is the handoff around the model: what enters the system, what evidence is available, who can approve the next action, and what happens when the output is uncertain.
I think of human review as a workflow state.
Do not begin with “where can we add an agent?” Begin with an event the team already recognizes:
a quote has received no response;
an invoice contains missing or contradictory fields;
a customer request needs a policy decision;
an order document does not match the expected format;
an email attachment needs to be entered into an existing system.
